    "name": "hornbeam",
    "notes": "THE BOLE LOOKS TWISTED UNDER TENSION, and the one parameter that would say it -- `trunk.lobes`, which runs vertical grooves up the trunk -- IS NOT SAFE AND IS LEFT AT ZERO. Its own help text says so: grooving the trunk severs the joins where limbs and roots attach and leaves wood floating, and four separate restrictions each reduced the damage and none removed it. Doing this properly means fluting the capsule as it is drawn rather than carving afterwards, and that is generator work.\n\nSo the hornbeam is authored on the other half of its identity: a short heavy bole with a very dense low crown starting under half its height, which is a different silhouette from the beech even without the fluting.",
